    "description": "- Defined and drove the company’s cross-platform strategy by architecting a Kotlin Multiplatform (KMP) shared module that unified Android and iOS business logic, reducing feature development cycles by ~33% and eliminating duplicated codepaths across 2 native clients\n- Owned end-to-end delivery of 15+ production features spanning Android, iOS, KMP, and Unity — including a multi-screen onboarding system (account creation, payments, permissions, appointment scheduling), real-time messaging, and deep linking infrastructure\n- Led root-cause investigation of a high-severity production defect affecting ~25–30% of the Android device fleet: traced silent audio failures to Unity memory management on low-RAM devices (≤4 GB), designed the diagnostic methodology, and enabled a targeted fix that restored session reliability at scale\n- Established engineering quality standards across the mobile org: implemented code review gates, KMP architecture guidelines, and performance benchmarking; mentored engineers on cross-platform best practices and progressive complexity ownership\n- Directed technical coordination across internal engineers and external Unity/Android contractors, aligning 3 concurrent codebases on shared release timelines and maximizing cross-team delivery velocity",
